A closure in JavaScript is a function that remembers the environment in which it was created. Here is a short example:

```javascript
function createCounter() {
  let count = 0;
  return function() {
    count++;
    return count;
  };
}

const counter1 = createCounter();
console.log(counter1()); // Output: 1
console.log(counter1()); // Output: 2
```

